  "chronology": [
    "The school archive dates the wooden pailou to 1898. A historic print shows a timber gateway with its high central plaque and two lower side openings.",
    "The university property administration records the 1934 donations and the 1935 reconstruction copying a Beijing palace entrance, with red doors and green glazed roofing. A university travel account published in 2005 specifies June 1935.",
    "The university archive places a concrete bridge at the former watercourse in 1926, backfilling in the early 1950s, and replacement symbolic stone lamp posts after the 1998 road widening. The model is limited to the gatehouse, the post-1935 front, and paired guardian plinths."
  ],
